  "id": "Compound::DB00835 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Brompheniramine, a nasal decongestant, is shown to bind to Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the arachidonic acid epoxygenase and monooxygenase pathways, which are ultimately linked to Cyp2e1. The evidence suggests that Brompheniramine may influence Cyp2e1 through the modulation of these metabolic pathways. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Brompheniramine and Cyp2e1, with the shared involvement of Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6 in arachidonic acid metabolism being a key mechanism. The observed interactions suggest that Brompheniramine could potentially modulate Cyp2e1 activity by affecting the enzymatic processes of arachidonic acid metabolism. The mechanism is supported by the presence of overlapping pathways and the consistent binding of Brompheniramine to these enzymes, which collectively point to a plausible, mechanistically grounded relationship between the drug and Cyp2e1.",
